2. Switching to renewable energy sources: This involves using renewable energy sources like solar, wind, and hydro power to generate electricity instead of fossil fuels. This can significantly reduce greenhouse gas emissions since renewable energy sources do not produce carbon dioxide or other greenhouse gases.
3. Carbon capture and storage: This involves capturing carbon dioxide emissions from industrial processes and storing them underground or in other storage facilities. This can help to reduce the amount of greenhouse gases that are released into the atmosphere.
